Category,Name,Variation,Rotation,Level,Lvl #,Builds From,Leads To,Terrain / Feature,Description,Also Known As,Review,Terrain
Carving,Railroad Tracks,,,Green,1.0,Linked skidded turns,Edge Roll,Groomed / Hardpack,Clean carved turns that leave two narrow parallel tracks — the board tips on edge and follows its sidecut with no lateral scrub.,,,
Flatground,Manual,Nose,,Green,1.0,Ollie,Nose Press / Tail Press,Flat,Maintain balance over one end of the board while the opposite end is lifted; requires precise fore-aft pressure control.,,,
Flatground,Manual,Tail,,Green,1.0,Ollie,Nose Press / Tail Press,Flat,Maintain balance over one end of the board while the opposite end is lifted; requires precise fore-aft pressure control.,,,
Flatground,Nollie,,,Green,1.0,Ollie,Manual,Flat,"Spring from the nose to lift the board, reversing the usual ollie pressure pattern.",,,
Flatground,Nose Press,,,Green,1.0,Manual,Butters,Flat / Box,Shift pressure toward the nose so the tail becomes light or lifted while maintaining board control.,,,
Flatground,Ollie,,,Green,1.0,Flat-base riding,Nollie,Flat,Spring from the tail to lift the board off the snow using coordinated flexion and extension to create pop.,,,
Flatground,Penguin Walk,,,Green,1.0,Wheelie,Tic-Tac,,Rapidly shifting weight between nose and tail to shuffle forward across flat ground without unstrapping — the standard fix for a dead-flat runout.,,,
Flatground,Stink Bug,,,Green,1.0,Indy,Cannonball,,"A tucked-back Indy: rear hand grabs the toe edge, but instead of a light tweak the board is pulled straight up toward the chest while the feet drive down and both knees bow outward.",,,
Flatground,Tail Press,,,Green,1.0,Manual,Butters,Flat / Box,Shift pressure toward the tail so the nose becomes light or lifted while maintaining board control.,,,
Flatground,Tic-Tac,,,Green,1.0,Penguin Walk,Frontside 180,,"Quickly pivoting the nose side to side while pushing off alternating edges to build speed on flat ground, borrowed directly from skateboarding.",,,
Flatground,Wheelie,,,Green,1.0,Manual,Tic-Tac,,Weight shifted back over the tail binding to lift the nose clear of the snow and hold it there while riding straight — a snowboard version of a bike wheelie.,,,
Freeride / Natural Terrain,Bank Turn,,,Green,1.0,Linked turns,Bank Slash,Bank / Natural Terrain,Using a natural bank to redirect the board while maintaining flow through the terrain.,,,
Freeride / Natural Terrain,Natural Ollie,,,Green,1.0,Ollie,Natural Air,Natural Terrain,Ollie performed from or over a natural terrain feature.,,,
Freeride / Natural Terrain,Side Hit,,,Green,1.0,Straight Air,Side-Hit Grab,Side Hit,Using a natural or trail-side lip as a jump rather than a purpose-built feature.,,,
Grabs,Cannonball,,,Green,1.0,Stink Bug,Straight Air,,Both hands grab the knees and pull them into a tight tuck. No tweak — the goal is to stay balled up for as much of the airtime as possible.,,,
Jumps,Fakie,,,Green,1.0,Linked turns,Switch,All,The rider goes backwards in their basic stance. The tail turns to nose,,,
Jumps,Ollie,,,Green,1.0,Flat-base riding,Nollie,Flat,A trick in which the snowboarder springs off the tail of the board and into the air.,,,
Jumps,Straight Air,,,Green,1.0,Ollie,Boned Air,Jump,"Leave the takeoff with a neutral board and body position, maintain stability in the air, and land with both feet aligned to the terrain.",,,
Rails / Boxes,50-50,,,Green,1.0,Straight glides on snow,Boardslide,Rail / Box,"Board travels parallel with the feature. Establish the feature position with a controlled entry, maintain pressure and balance through the feature, and exit cleanly.",,,
Carving,Carve Slash,,,Blue,2.0,Short Carve,High Edge-Angle Carve,Groomed / Hardpack,Aggressive release of a carved turn that redirects the board and throws a spray of snow.,"Carve Spray, Slasher Bombs",,
Carving,Edge Roll,,,Blue,2.0,Railroad Tracks,Snake Turns,,"Rolling the board smoothly from one edge to the other while traveling across the hill — isolating the edge-change itself, driven by the ankles and knees, before it gets linked into a full turn.",,,
Carving,Long Carve,,,Blue,2.0,Snake Turns,Short Carve,Groomed / Hardpack,"Long-radius carved turn held across the fall line, using a patient edge change and sustained edge engagement.",,,
Carving,Short Carve,,,Blue,2.0,Long Carve,Speed Carve,Groomed / Hardpack,"Tight-radius carved turns driven by angulation — bending at the ankles, knees and hips to tip the board onto edge while the upper body stays quiet, rather than leaning the whole body. Shorter and quicker than a Long Carve, and the technique that everything from Speed Carve to the drag carves is built on.",,,
Carving,Snake Turns,,,Blue,2.0,Edge Roll,Long Carve,,"Quick, linked carved turns down the fall line in a tight rhythmic S-shape, like a snake track — driven by ankle and knee articulation rather than a full-body rotation. The standard drill for dialing in edge-change timing before stretching turns out into a Long Carve.",Carved Snake Turns,,
Carving,Speed Carve,,,Blue,2.0,Short Carve,High Edge-Angle Carve,Groomed / Hardpack,"Carving to build speed rather than hold it: the rider pumps through the transition and drives the body across the board edge to edge, extending out of the turn to accelerate. Distinct from simply holding a long edge, which sheds speed through turn shape.",,,
Flatground,Bonk,,,Blue,2.0,Ollie,Natural Bonk,Flat / Feature,"Use contact with an object or feature to redirect, pivot, or pop the board rather than simply riding over it.",Bonk/Tap,"Source gave no real description — category, level and progression are my best guess.",
Flatground,Butter Bagel,,,Blue,2.0,Flatland Pretzel,Tailslide 270 Out,,"Nollie into a tail butter, spin the board sideways, then release in the same direction the spin started — one continuous circular motion with no reversal, bridging pure buttering and rail riding.",,,
Flatground,Butters,Tail,,Blue,2.0,Nose Press / Tail Press,Nose Roll / Tail Roll,Flat,Use flex and pressure over one end of the board to pivot or rotate while keeping the board engaged with the snow.,,,
Flatground,Butters,Nose,,Blue,2.0,Nose Press / Tail Press,Nose Roll / Tail Roll,Flat,Use flex and pressure over one end of the board to pivot or rotate while keeping the board engaged with the snow.,,,
Flatground,Drive Spin,,,Blue,2.0,Nose Press,Frontside Powder Roll,,"A backside nose-butter spin driven by two rotations fired in sequence — the upper body unwinds first, then the lower body scissors through — which makes it noticeably faster than a standard butter spin.",,,
Flatground,Flat Spin 360,,,Blue,2.0,Surface Spin,Frontside 360,,"A full 360 done entirely on the snow with no pop: a Backside 180 flows straight into a switch Frontside 180 with no stop between them, using edge control alone to complete the rotation.",,,
Flatground,Flatland Pretzel,,,Blue,2.0,Nose Press,Butter Bagel,,"On-snow pretzel: frontside 90 degrees into a heel-edge nose press, then spring out backside 270 degrees into a switch toeside carve — twisted entry, opposite exit.",,,
Flatground,Frontside Powder Roll,,,Blue,2.0,Drive Spin,Tail Butter Frontside 180,,"A frontside 180 into a switch tail press, then a switch backside 180 back out — two spins linked through one butter. Despite the name it is usually drilled on groomers first, not powder.",,,
Flatground,Hand Drag,,,Blue,2.0,Tripod,Tuck Knee,Flat,Hand drag variation.,,,
Flatground,High Press,,,Blue,2.0,Tail Press,Hot Garbage,,A one-footed tail press with the front foot lifted and the tail driven as deep as possible — the base position that becomes a Bluntslide once a counter-rotated shifty is added.,,,
Flatground,Hot Garbage,,,Blue,2.0,Slash Pop,High Press,,"An on-snow blunt thrown off a roller or knuckle: ollie over the crest, drag the dipped tail on the snow, and twist it into a held backside shifty.",,,
Flatground,Layback Tail Press,,,Blue,2.0,Tail Press,Tripod,,"Riding straight with the hips dropped all the way to the snow, arms out and head facing downhill, while balanced on the tail.",,,
Flatground,Nose Roll,FS,,Blue,2.0,Butters,Nose Roll (BS),,"Frontside nose roll: carve in on the heel edge, pivot 180 degrees over the nose, and ride away switch on the heel edge — heel to heel the whole way through.",,,
Flatground,Nose Roll,BS,,Blue,2.0,Nose Roll (FS),Tail Roll (FS),,"Backside nose roll: carve in on the toe edge, pivot 180 degrees over the nose, and exit switch on the toe edge, keeping one edge committed from entry to exit.",,,
Flatground,Slash Pop,,,Blue,2.0,Carve Slash,Hot Garbage,,"A hard tail-first carve into a roller or knuckle, close to a high press with a shifty motion added, timed so the pitch of the feature makes the rider weightless as they pop off it.",,,
Flatground,Tail Butter Backside 180,,,Blue,2.0,Tail Butter Frontside 180,Backside 180 Butter Frontside 180,,"Nollie into a tail press, chest twists toward the tail while the eyes stay forward, then one pop releases into a blind backside 180 landing.",,,
Flatground,Tail Butter Frontside 180,,,Blue,2.0,Frontside Powder Roll,Frontside 180 Butter Backside 180,,"Nollie into a tail press, chest opens through the press, then one pop unwinds the stored rotation into a frontside 180 landing regular.",,,
Flatground,Tail Roll,FS,,Blue,2.0,Nose Roll (BS),Tail Roll (BS),,"Frontside tail roll: carve in on the heel edge, pivot 180 degrees over the tail, and ride away switch on the heel edge, with a slight twist toward the hill through the press.",,,
Flatground,Tail Roll,BS,,Blue,2.0,Tail Roll (FS),Noseroll Nollie 360,,"Backside tail roll: carve in on the toe edge, pivot 180 degrees over the tail, and exit switch on the toe edge, staying committed to one edge throughout.",,,
Flatground,Tripod,,,Blue,2.0,Butters,Hand Drag,Flat,"Lower the body and use a hand contact with the snow to support a low, controlled balance position.",,,
Flips / Inverted,Tamedog,,,Blue,2.0,Frontflip,Frontflip to Fakie,,"A frontflip performed off a straight jump with no added rotation, board staying perpendicular to the fall line throughout — the frontflip counterpart to a Wildcat.",,,
Freeride / Natural Terrain,Bank Slash,,,Blue,2.0,Bank Turn,,Bank / Natural Terrain,Aggressively releasing or redirecting the board from a natural bank while creating a spray.,,,
Freeride / Natural Terrain,Natural Air,,,Blue,2.0,Natural Ollie,Natural Tweak,Natural Terrain,"Straight air performed from a natural lip, roller, bank, or other terrain feature.",,,
Freeride / Natural Terrain,Natural Bonk,,,Blue,2.0,Bonk,Rock Bonk,Natural Terrain,"Using a natural object or terrain feature to contact, redirect, or pop the board.",,,
Freeride / Natural Terrain,Natural Nollie,,,Blue,2.0,Nollie,Natural Air,Natural Terrain,Nollie performed from or over a natural terrain feature.,,,
Freeride / Natural Terrain,Natural Shifty,,,Blue,2.0,Shifty,Cliff Shifty,Natural Terrain,Rotating the board independently from the upper body during an air from natural terrain.,,,
Freeride / Natural Terrain,Side-Hit 180,,180°,Blue,2.0,Side-Hit Grab,Side-Hit 360,Side Hit,180° performed from a side hit.,,,
Freeride / Natural Terrain,Side-Hit Grab,,,Blue,2.0,Side Hit,Side-Hit 180,Side Hit,Adding a grab to an air performed from a side hit.,,,
Grabs,Boned Air,,,Blue,2.0,Straight Air,Tweaked Air,Jump,Extend the board away from the body. Perform the movement during the airborne phase while maintaining control of the board and preparing for a balanced landing.,,,
Grabs,Gorilla,,,Blue,2.0,Indy,Beef Carpaccio,Jump,Both hands grab toeside between the bindings.,,,
Grabs,Indy,Rear hand toeside between bindings,,Blue,2.0,Straight Air,Melon,Jump,"Secure the board with the indicated hand and contact point while airborne. Maintain the grab long enough to clearly establish the position, then release it in time to prepare for landing.",,,
Grabs,Melon,Front hand heelside between bindings,,Blue,2.0,Indy,Mute,Jump,"Secure the board with the indicated hand and contact point while airborne. Maintain the grab long enough to clearly establish the position, then release it in time to prepare for landing.",,,
Grabs,Mute,Front hand toeside between bindings,,Blue,2.0,Melon,Stalefish,Jump,"Secure the board with the indicated hand and contact point while airborne. Maintain the grab long enough to clearly establish the position, then release it in time to prepare for landing.",,,
Grabs,Nose Boned,,,Blue,2.0,Nose Grab,Tweaked Air,Jump,Nose extended away from the body. Perform the movement during the airborne phase while maintaining control of the board and preparing for a balanced landing.,,,
Grabs,Nose Grab,Front hand on nose,,Blue,2.0,Tail Grab,Melon,Jump,"Secure the board with the indicated hand and contact point while airborne. Maintain the grab long enough to clearly establish the position, then release it in time to prepare for landing.",,,
Grabs,Sad,,,Blue,2.0,Nose Grab,Rocket Air,Jump,"Similar to Nosebone, but grabbing with front hand heel side, and the nose points to the ground.",Sad Air,,
Grabs,Slob Air,,,Blue,2.0,Weddle,Tai Pan,Jump,"The front hand grabs Weddle, the back leg is boned and the board is kept parallel with the ground.",,,
Grabs,Stalefish,Rear hand heelside between bindings,,Blue,2.0,Mute,Roast Beef,Jump,"Secure the board with the indicated hand and contact point while airborne. Maintain the grab long enough to clearly establish the position, then release it in time to prepare for landing.",,,
Grabs,Stiffy,,,Blue,2.0,Boned Air,Tweaked Air,Jump,Legs extended while grabbing. Perform the movement during the airborne phase while maintaining control of the board and preparing for a balanced landing.,,,
Grabs,Tail Boned,,,Blue,2.0,Tail Grab,Tweaked Air,Jump,Tail extended away from the body. Perform the movement during the airborne phase while maintaining control of the board and preparing for a balanced landing.,,,
Grabs,Tail Grab,Rear hand on tail,,Blue,2.0,Straight Air,Nose Grab,Jump,"Secure the board with the indicated hand and contact point while airborne. Maintain the grab long enough to clearly establish the position, then release it in time to prepare for landing.",,,
Grabs,Tailfish,,,Blue,2.0,Stalefish,Fresh Fish,Jump,Big Air variation.,,,
Grabs,Tindy,,,Blue,2.0,Indy,Tail Grab,Jump,Grab variation.,,,
Grabs,Tuck Knee,,,Blue,2.0,Indy,Weddle,Jump,A technique where one knee is bent and the ankle bent sideways to touch the knee to the snowboard between the bindings.,,,
Grabs,Weddle,,,Blue,2.0,Mute,Slob Air,Jump,The front hand grabs the toe edge either between the toes or in front of the front foot.,,,
Jumps,BS 180,Backside,180,Blue,2.0,Straight Air / Shifty,BS 360,Jump / Feature,"Complete a 180-degree backside rotation while airborne, controlling takeoff, axis, spotting, and landing throughout the spin.",,,
Jumps,BS 360,Backside,360,Blue,2.0,BS 180,BS 540,Jump / Feature,"Complete a 360-degree backside rotation while airborne, controlling takeoff, axis, spotting, and landing throughout the spin.",,,
Jumps,BS Shifty,,,Blue,2.0,Shifty,BS 180,Jump,"Counter-rotate the upper and lower body in the air, changing the board's orientation without completing a full rotation.",,,
Jumps,Butter,,,Blue,2.0,Nose Press / Tail Press,Nose Roll,Flat,Use flex and pressure over one end of the board to pivot or rotate while keeping the board engaged with the snow.,,,
Jumps,FS 180,Frontside,180,Blue,2.0,Straight Air / Shifty,FS 360,Jump / Feature,"Complete a 180-degree frontside rotation while airborne, controlling takeoff, axis, spotting, and landing throughout the spin.",,,
Jumps,FS 360,Frontside,360,Blue,2.0,FS 180,FS 540,Jump / Feature,"Complete a 360-degree frontside rotation while airborne, controlling takeoff, axis, spotting, and landing throughout the spin.",,,
Jumps,FS Shifty,,,Blue,2.0,Shifty,FS 180,Jump,"Counter-rotate the upper and lower body in the air, changing the board's orientation without completing a full rotation.",,,
Jumps,Half Cab,,180.0,Blue,2.0,Switch,Switch Backside 180,,"Switch frontside 180: take off from switch stance, rotate frontside 180 degrees, and land regular. The building block for the whole Cab family.",,,
Jumps,Revert,BS,180,Blue,2.0,Pivot slips,BS 180,Snow,"Rotate the board on the snow through 180 degrees to change riding direction, finishing in the opposite stance/orientation.",Revert Carve,,
Jumps,Revert,FS,180,Blue,2.0,Pivot slips,BS 180,Snow,"Rotate the board on the snow through 180 degrees to change riding direction, finishing in the opposite stance/orientation.",Revert Carve,,
Jumps,Shifty,,,Blue,2.0,Straight Air,FS Shifty / BS Shifty,Jump / Flat,"Counter-rotate the upper and lower body in the air, changing the board's orientation without completing a full rotation.",,,
Jumps,Switch,,,Blue,2.0,Fakie,Cab,All,"The rider goes backwards with their stance switched. A regular rider now goes like a goofy rider, and vice versa.",,,
Jumps,Switch Backside 180,,180.0,Blue,2.0,Half Cab,Switch Backside 360,,"A 180 taken off from switch stance and rotated backside, landing regular.",,,
Pipe / Transition,Air,,,Blue,2.0,Drop-in + pumping the pipe,FS Air / BS Air,Halfpipe,"Straight air from transition. Use the transition to create vertical airtime and manage the board/body relationship through takeoff, apex, and landing.",,,
Pipe / Transition,Air to Fakie,,180,Blue,2.0,Straight Air,BS 180 to Fakie,Halfpipe,Land riding switch. Perform the movement during the airborne phase while maintaining control of the board and preparing for a balanced landing.,,,
Pipe / Transition,Air-to-fakie,,,Blue,2.0,Air,Poptart,Halfpipe,"Any trick in the halfpipe/quarterpipes where the wall is approached riding forward, no rotation is made, and the snowboarder lands riding backward.",,,
Pipe / Transition,BS 180,,180,Blue,2.0,BS Air,BS 360,Halfpipe,"Backside rotation in pipe. Use the transition to create vertical airtime and manage the board/body relationship through takeoff, apex, and landing.",,,
Pipe / Transition,BS Air,,,Blue,2.0,Air,BS 180,Halfpipe,"Backside air. Use the transition to create vertical airtime and manage the board/body relationship through takeoff, apex, and landing.",,,
Pipe / Transition,FS 180,,180,Blue,2.0,FS Air,FS 360,Halfpipe,"Frontside rotation in pipe. Use the transition to create vertical airtime and manage the board/body relationship through takeoff, apex, and landing.",,,
Pipe / Transition,FS Air,,,Blue,2.0,Air,FS 180,Halfpipe,"Frontside air. Use the transition to create vertical airtime and manage the board/body relationship through takeoff, apex, and landing.",,,
Pipe / Transition,Poptart,,,Blue,2.0,Air-to-fakie,FS Air,Halfpipe,Airing from fakie to forward in the halfpipe without rotation.,,,
Powder,Powder 180,,180°,Blue,2.0,Powder Hop,Powder 360,Powder / Natural Terrain,180° rotation performed while riding or popping through powder.,,,
Powder,Powder Hop,,,Blue,2.0,Powder Surf,Powder 180,Powder / Off-Piste,"Small hop used to change edges, redirect the board, or adjust the line in deeper snow.",,,
Powder,Powder Slash,,,Blue,2.0,Slash Turn,Powder Spray,Powder / Off-Piste,Aggressive edge engagement that redirects the board and throws a large spray of snow.,,,
Powder,Powder Spray,,,Blue,2.0,Powder Slash,Bank Slash,Powder / Off-Piste,Intentionally creating a large spray of snow through a strong turn or slash.,,,
Powder,Powder Surf,,,Blue,2.0,Slash Turn,Powder Butter,Deep Powder,"Fluid, surf-style riding that uses the board's float and the resistance of deep snow to shape turns.",,,
Powder,Slash Turn,,,Blue,2.0,Linked turns off-piste,Powder Slash,Powder / Off-Piste,"Short, powerful turn that uses edge pressure and snow resistance to redirect the board.",,,
Rails / Boxes,Boardslide,,,Blue,2.0,50-50,Lipslide,Rail / Box,The rider slides sideways at a 90-degree angle with the rail between the bindings. FS performed from frontside approach; BS from backside approach.,,,
Rails / Boxes,Boardslide,FS,,Blue,2.0,50-50,Lipslide,Rail / Box,Board is perpendicular to the feature; FS approach. Maintain a centered controlled slide position rather than catching an edge.,,,
Rails / Boxes,Boardslide,BS,,Blue,2.0,50-50,Lipslide,Rail / Box,Board is perpendicular to the feature; BS approach. Maintain a centered controlled slide position rather than catching an edge.,,,
Rails / Boxes,Lipslide,,,Blue,2.0,Boardslide,Noseslide,Rail / Box,"A slide where the rider's trailing foot passes over the rail on approach, with the snowboard traveling perpendicular along the rail.",,,
Rails / Boxes,Lipslide,FS,,Blue,2.0,Boardslide,Noseslide,Rail / Box,Frontside lipslide. Maintain a centered controlled slide position rather than catching an edge.,,,
Rails / Boxes,Lipslide,BS,,Blue,2.0,Boardslide,Noseslide,Rail / Box,Backside lipslide. Maintain a centered controlled slide position rather than catching an edge.,,,
Rails / Boxes,Nosepress,,,Blue,2.0,Nose Press on snow,Noseslide,Rail / Box,Press over the nose while sliding. Establish the feature position with a controlled entry; maintain pressure and balance through the feature and exit cleanly.,,,
Rails / Boxes,Noseslide,BS,,Blue,2.0,Boardslide,Tailslide,Rail / Box,Nose leads the slide from the opposite approach. Establish the feature position with a controlled entry; maintain pressure and balance through the feature and exit cleanly.,,,
Rails / Boxes,Noseslide,FS,,Blue,2.0,Boardslide,Tailslide,Rail / Box,Nose leads the slide. Establish the feature position with a controlled entry; maintain pressure and balance through the feature and exit cleanly.,,,
Rails / Boxes,Noseslide,,,Blue,2.0,Boardslide,Tailslide,Rail / Box,Nose leads the slide along the feature.,,,
Rails / Boxes,Tailpress,,,Blue,2.0,Tail Press on snow,Tailslide,Rail / Box,Press over the tail while sliding. Establish the feature position with a controlled entry; maintain pressure and balance through the feature and exit cleanly.,,,
Rails / Boxes,Tailslide,BS,,Blue,2.0,Noseslide,Bluntslide,Rail / Box,Tail leads the slide from the opposite approach. Establish the feature position with a controlled entry; maintain pressure and balance through the feature and exit cleanly.,,,
Rails / Boxes,Tailslide,FS,,Blue,2.0,Noseslide,Bluntslide,Rail / Box,Tail leads the slide. Establish the feature position with a controlled entry; maintain pressure and balance through the feature and exit cleanly.,,,
Rails / Boxes,Tailslide,,,Blue,2.0,Noseslide,Bluntslide,Rail / Box,Tail leads the slide along the feature.,,,
Carving,Carve Drag,Hand,,Black,3.0,High Edge-Angle Carve,Carve Drag (knee),Groomed / Hardpack,"Trailing a hand across the snow through a high edge-angle carve — the first and safest contact point, and a useful check on edge angle.",,,
Carving,Carve Drag,Knee,,Black,3.0,Carve Drag (hand),Carve Drag (hip),Groomed / Hardpack,"Lowering the knee to the snow through a deep carve, which demands more inclination and a lower stance than a hand drag.",,,
Carving,Carve Drag,Hip,,Black,3.0,Carve Drag (knee),Carve Drag (elbow),Groomed / Hardpack,Bringing the hip to the snow through the belly of the turn; requires enough edge angle to support the body at that inclination.,,,
Carving,High Edge-Angle Carve,,,Black,3.0,Speed Carve,Carve Drag (hand),Groomed / Hardpack,"Carving at a large edge angle for maximum grip and a narrow turn track, using angulation at the hips and knees to keep the body stacked over the edge.",Deep Carve,,
Features / Transition,Disaster,,,Black,3.0,50-50,Stall,Transition,"Land with the board crossing the lip/feature. The feature or transition changes the available takeoff, landing, or balance demands, so approach speed and body position must be matched to the terrain.",,,
Features / Transition,Quarterpipe Air,,,Black,3.0,Straight Air,Quarterpipe FS,Quarterpipe,"Air off a quarterpipe-style transition. The feature or transition changes the available takeoff, landing, or balance demands, so approach speed and body position must be matched to the terrain.",,,
Features / Transition,Quarterpipe BS,,,Black,3.0,Quarterpipe FS,Handplant,Quarterpipe,"Backside trick off transition. The feature or transition changes the available takeoff, landing, or balance demands, so approach speed and body position must be matched to the terrain.",,,
Features / Transition,Quarterpipe FS,,,Black,3.0,Quarterpipe Air,Quarterpipe BS,Quarterpipe,"Frontside trick off transition. The feature or transition changes the available takeoff, landing, or balance demands, so approach speed and body position must be matched to the terrain.",,,
Features / Transition,Stall,Nose,,Black,3.0,50-50,Disaster,Rail / Wall / Transition,"Pause or balance on the nose. The feature or transition changes the available takeoff, landing, or balance demands, so approach speed and body position must be matched to the terrain.",,,
Features / Transition,Stall,Tail,,Black,3.0,50-50,Disaster,Rail / Wall / Transition,"Pause or balance on the tail. The feature or transition changes the available takeoff, landing, or balance demands, so approach speed and body position must be matched to the terrain.",,,
Features / Transition,Transfer,FS,,Black,3.0,50-50,Boardslide to Boardslide,Transition / Jump,"Move across the feature in a frontside direction. The feature or transition changes the available takeoff, landing, or balance demands, so approach speed and body position must be matched to the terrain.",,,
Features / Transition,Transfer,BS,,Black,3.0,50-50,Boardslide to Boardslide,Transition / Jump,"Move across the feature in a backside direction. The feature or transition changes the available takeoff, landing, or balance demands, so approach speed and body position must be matched to the terrain.",,,
Flatground,Backside 180 Butter Frontside 180,,,Black,3.0,Tail Butter Backside 180,Frontside 180-In 360-Out,,"Backside 180 into a switch tail press, held briefly, then a snappy frontside 180 back to regular — harder than the frontside-first version and the standard entry for the same trick in powder.",,,
Flatground,Backside 180-In 360-Out,,,Black,3.0,Frontside Tailroll 360,Frontside 180-In 360-Out,,"Backside 180 into a tail butter, then a switch frontside 360 out — one extra rotation added to the basic 180-in-180-out butter on the exit.",,,
Flatground,Backside Noseroll 360,,,Black,3.0,Nollie Backside 360,Frontside Tailroll 360,,"A backside nose roll taken past 180 all the way through a full 360: starts on the toe edge, crosses to the heel edge at the halfway point, and rides away on a heelside carve.",,,
Flatground,Frontside 180 Butter Backside 180,,,Black,3.0,Tail Butter Frontside 180,Backside 180-In 360-Out,,"Frontside 180 into a switch tail press, held briefly, then a counter-rotated backside 180 back to regular — the butter links two spins in opposite directions.",,,
Flatground,Frontside 180-In 360-Out,,,Black,3.0,Backside 180-In 360-Out,Backside 540 Noseroll,,"Frontside 180 into a tail butter with the upper body continuing to wind through the press, then one release into a switch backside 360 — harder than the opposite direction because of the switch-backside exit.",,,
Flatground,Frontside Tailroll 360,,,Black,3.0,Backside Noseroll 360,Backside 180-In 360-Out,,"A heelside tail press carried all the way through a full frontside 360, smooth and continuous from entry to exit.",,,
Flatground,Nollie Backside 180,,,Black,3.0,Noseroll Nollie 360,Nollie Backside 360,,"Toeside carve into a nose press, then an explosive pop off the front foot backside, landing switch on the toe edge.",,,
Flatground,Nollie Backside 360,,,Black,3.0,Nollie Backside 180,Backside Noseroll 360,,A nollie carried through a full backside 360 rather than stopping at 180.,,,
Flatground,Noseroll Nollie 360,,,Black,3.0,Nose Roll (FS),Nollie Backside 180,,"A frontside nose roll carried past 180 degrees all the way around to a full 360, with the head and shoulders leading the extra rotation instead of stopping at the halfway point.",,,
Flips / Inverted,Barrel Roll,,,Black,3.0,Straight Air,Backflip,,A flip taken over the toe or heel edge rather than nose-over-tail — a sideways somersault instead of a forward or backward one.,,,
Freeride / Natural Terrain,Cliff Air,,,Black,3.0,Cliff Drop,Cliff Grab,Cliff / Natural Terrain,Adding an aerial maneuver or body movement to a cliff drop.,,,
Freeride / Natural Terrain,Cliff Drop,,,Black,3.0,Natural Drop,Cliff Air,Cliff / Natural Terrain,Dropping from a natural cliff or significant vertical feature and landing below.,,,
Freeride / Natural Terrain,Natural Drop,,,Black,3.0,Natural Air,Cliff Drop,Natural Terrain,Riding or jumping from a natural change in elevation onto lower terrain.,,,
Freeride / Natural Terrain,Natural Tweak,,,Black,3.0,Natural Air,Cliff Grab,Natural Terrain,Deliberately manipulating the board and body position during a natural air for style or control.,,,
Freeride / Natural Terrain,Rock Bonk,,,Black,3.0,Natural Bonk,Tree Bonk,Rocks / Natural Terrain,Using a rock or exposed natural feature as a bonk or takeoff.,,,
Freeride / Natural Terrain,Side-Hit 360,,360°,Black,3.0,Side-Hit 180,Banked 360,Side Hit,360° performed from a side hit.,,,
Freeride / Natural Terrain,Tree Bonk,,,Black,3.0,Rock Bonk,—,Trees / Natural Terrain,"Using a tree as a natural feature to tap, redirect, or initiate an aerial maneuver.",,,
Grabs,Bloody Dracula,,,Black,3.0,Tail Grab,Holy Crail,Jump,A trick in which the rider grabs the tail of the board with both hands. The rear hand grabs the board as it would during a regular tail-grab but the front hand blindly reaches for the board behind the rider's back.,,,
Grabs,Canada Bacon,,,Black,3.0,Roast Beef,Beef Curtains,Jump,The rear hand reaches behind the rear leg to grab the toe edge between the bindings while the rear leg is boned.,Canadian Bacon,,
Grabs,Chicken Salad,,,Black,3.0,Roast Beef,Swiss Cheese Air,Jump,The rear hand reaches between the legs and grabs the heel edge between the bindings while the front leg is boned. The wrist is rotated inward to complete the grab.,,,
Grabs,China Air,,,Black,3.0,Mute,Japan,Jump,An easier version of the Japan Air; the front hand grabs the toe side in front of the front foot. Both knees are then bent.,,,
Grabs,Crail,Rear hand on nose,,Black,3.0,Nose Grab,Holy Crail,Jump,"Secure the board with the indicated hand and contact point while airborne. Maintain the grab long enough to clearly establish the position, then release it in time to prepare for landing.",,,
Grabs,Cross Rocket,,,Black,3.0,Rocket Air,Double Tail,,"A two-handed nose grab with the hands crossed to opposite sides of the nose, rear leg boned straight — the crossed-arm version of a Rocket Air.",,,
Grabs,Double Tail,,,Black,3.0,Cross Rocket,Cookie Monster,,"Both hands grab the tail together, front hand reaching across the body the way it would for a Seatbelt.",,,
Grabs,Fresh Fish,,,Black,3.0,Stalefish,Chicken Salad,Jump,The backside version of the stale fish.,,,
Grabs,Holy Crail,,,Black,3.0,Crail,Bloody Dracula,Jump,Crail variation.,,,
Grabs,Japan,Mute grab with a frontside shifty and arching back,,Black,3.0,Mute,Method,Jump,"Secure the board with the indicated hand and contact point while airborne. Maintain the grab long enough to clearly establish the position, then release it in time to prepare for landing.",Japan Air,,
Grabs,Lien,,,Black,3.0,Melon,Method,Jump,"When performing a frontside air on transition, the snowboarder grabs heelside in front or behind the leading binding with their leading hand.",,,
Grabs,Method,Melon grab with a backside shifty and poking the tail,,Black,3.0,Melon,Japan,Jump,"Secure the board with the indicated hand and contact point while airborne. Maintain the grab long enough to clearly establish the position, then release it in time to prepare for landing.",,,
Grabs,Roast Beef,Rear hand between legs on heel edge,,Black,3.0,Stalefish,Chicken Salad,Jump,"Secure the board with the indicated hand and contact point while airborne. Maintain the grab long enough to clearly establish the position, then release it in time to prepare for landing.",,,
Grabs,Rocket Air,,,Black,3.0,Nose Grab,Sad,Jump,Both hands grab the nose of the board.,,,
Grabs,Seatbelt,Front hand on tail,,Black,3.0,Tail Grab,Crail,Jump,"Secure the board with the indicated hand and contact point while airborne. Maintain the grab long enough to clearly establish the position, then release it in time to prepare for landing.",,,
Grabs,Spaghetti,,,Black,3.0,Roast Beef,Rusty Trombone,Jump,Grab variation.,,,
Grabs,Stelmasky,,,Black,3.0,Indy / Melon,—,Jump,"Front hand reaches through the legs from the front and grabs the heel edge between the bindings; the classic tweak bones out the back leg, similar to a Roast Beef. Dates to the 1980s, credited to skateboarder Mike Stelmasky, who first grabbed this position mid-handplant.",,,
Grabs,Suitcase,,,Black,3.0,Roast Beef,Cross Rocket,,"Front hand reaches around from behind the legs and grabs the toe edge between the feet, pulling the board straight up like lifting a suitcase while the back arches.",,,
Grabs,Tai Pan,,,Black,3.0,Indy,China Air,Jump,The back hand grabs the toe edge just in front of the rear foot with the arm going around the outside of the rear knee.,,,
Grabs,Tweaked Air,,,Black,3.0,Boned Air,Method,Jump,Grab with deliberate board/body tweak. Perform the movement during the airborne phase while maintaining control of the board and preparing for a balanced landing.,,,
Jumps,BS 540,Backside,540,Black,3.0,BS 360,BS 720,Jump / Feature,"Complete a 540-degree backside rotation while airborne, controlling takeoff, axis, spotting, and landing throughout the spin.",,,
Jumps,BS 720,Backside,720,Black,3.0,BS 540,BS 900,Jump / Feature,"Complete a 720-degree backside rotation while airborne, controlling takeoff, axis, spotting, and landing throughout the spin.",,,
Jumps,Cab,,360.0,Black,3.0,Switch,Cab 360,Jump / Feature,"Any switch-frontside spin (no matter the amount of rotation) on any feature (halfpipe, jumps, rails, boxes).",,,
Jumps,Cab 540,,540.0,Black,3.0,Cab,Cab 720,,"Switch frontside 540: one and a half rotations from switch stance, landing switch.",,,
Jumps,FS 540,Frontside,540,Black,3.0,FS 360,FS 720,Jump / Feature,"Complete a 540-degree frontside rotation while airborne, controlling takeoff, axis, spotting, and landing throughout the spin.",,,
Jumps,FS 720,Frontside,720,Black,3.0,FS 540,FS 900,Jump / Feature,"Complete a 720-degree frontside rotation while airborne, controlling takeoff, axis, spotting, and landing throughout the spin.",,,
Jumps,Switch Backside 360,,260.0,Black,3.0,Switch Backside 180,Switch Backside 540,,"A full 360 taken off from switch stance and rotated backside, landing regular — the backside counterpart to Cab.",,,
Jumps,Switch Backside 540,,,Black,3.0,Switch Backside 360,Switch Backside 720,,"Two and a quarter rotations from switch stance, rotating backside — the switch-backside counterpart to Cab 540.",Swack 540,,
Jumps,Tailbutter,,,Black,3.0,Butters,Tailfish,Big Air,Big Air variation.,,"Source gave no real description — category, level and progression are my best guess.",
Off-Axis Spins,BS Cork 540,,540,Black,3.0,BS 540,BS Cork 720,Jump,"540-degree backside off-axis spin. At takeoff the torso is tipped uphill of the feet, so the rotation leaves the vertical axis and the board passes overhead. Control the axis through the rotation and bring the board back level for the landing.",,,
Off-Axis Spins,BS Rodeo 540,,540,Black,3.0,BS 540,BS Rodeo 720,Jump,"540-degree backside off-axis spin. At takeoff the torso drops downhill of the feet, sending the rider backwards over the nose into the off-axis rotation. Control the axis through the rotation and bring the board back level for the landing.",,,
Off-Axis Spins,Cork,Generic,,Black,3.0,FS 540 / BS 540,FS Cork 540,Jump,"Off-axis spin family. At takeoff the torso is tipped uphill of the feet, so the rotation leaves the vertical axis and the board passes overhead. Direction and degree of rotation should be specified (e.g. FS Cork 720).",,,
Off-Axis Spins,FS Cork 540,,540,Black,3.0,FS 540,FS Cork 720,Jump,"540-degree frontside off-axis spin. At takeoff the torso is tipped uphill of the feet, so the rotation leaves the vertical axis and the board passes overhead. Control the axis through the rotation and bring the board back level for the landing.",,,
Off-Axis Spins,FS Rodeo 540,,540,Black,3.0,FS 540,FS Rodeo 720,Jump,"540-degree frontside off-axis spin. At takeoff the torso drops downhill of the feet, sending the rider backwards over the nose into the off-axis rotation. Control the axis through the rotation and bring the board back level for the landing.",,,
Off-Axis Spins,Rodeo,Generic,,Black,3.0,FS 540 / BS 540,FS Rodeo 540,Jump,"Off-axis spin family. At takeoff the torso drops downhill of the feet, sending the rider backwards over the nose into the off-axis rotation. Direction and degree of rotation should be specified (e.g. BS Rodeo 540).",,,
Pipe / Transition,Alley Oop,,,Black,3.0,FS Air,FS 360,Halfpipe,"A term used to describe any manoeuvre in the halfpipe/quarterpipe where one rotates 180 or more degrees in an uphill direction; rotating backside on the frontside wall, or rotating frontside on the backside wall.",,,
Pipe / Transition,BS 360,,360,Black,3.0,BS 180,BS 540,Halfpipe,"Backside rotation in pipe. Use the transition to create vertical airtime and manage the board/body relationship through takeoff, apex, and landing.",,,
Pipe / Transition,FS 360,,360,Black,3.0,FS 180,FS 540,Halfpipe,"Frontside rotation in pipe. Use the transition to create vertical airtime and manage the board/body relationship through takeoff, apex, and landing.",,,
Powder,Powder 360,,360°,Black,3.0,Powder 180,Powder 540+,Powder / Natural Terrain,Full 360° rotation performed in powder or soft off-piste snow.,,,
Powder,Powder Butter,,,Black,3.0,Powder Nose Press / Tail Press,Powder Roll,Powder,A butter performed in soft snow using the resistance of powder to support the maneuver.,,,
Powder,Powder Re-entry,,,Black,3.0,Powder Hop,Natural Air,Powder / Natural Terrain,Leaving the snow from a feature and landing back into a powder line.,,,
Powder,Powder Roll,,,Black,3.0,Powder 180,Powder 360,Deep Powder,Rolling the board through a directional or rotational movement while using the powder for support.,,,
Rails / Boxes,450 Off,,,Black,3.0,Bluntslide Pretzel 270 / Sameway 270,—,,Exiting a rail with one and a quarter rotations (450 degrees) rather than the standard 270 — one notch further on the same exit-rotation family.,,,
Rails / Boxes,BS Boardslide Pull Back,,90,Black,3.0,BS Boardslide,BS Boardslide to Fakie,Rail / Box,"Enter in a backside boardslide, maintain balance through the slide, then rotate 90 degrees back to regular stance facing down the hill.",,,
Rails / Boxes,BS Boardslide to Fakie,,90,Black,3.0,BS Boardslide Pull Back,BS Boardslide Sameway 270,Rail / Box,"Enter in a backside boardslide, maintain balance through the slide, then rotate 90 degrees to land fakie facing down the hill.",,,
Rails / Boxes,BS Lipslide Pull Back,,90,Black,3.0,BS Lipslide,BS Lipslide to Fakie,Rail / Box,"Enter in a backside lipslide, maintain balance through the slide, then rotate 90 degrees back to regular stance facing down the hill.",,,
Rails / Boxes,BS Lipslide to Fakie,,90,Black,3.0,BS Lipslide Pull Back,BS Lipslide Sameway 270,Rail / Box,"Enter in a backside lipslide, maintain balance through the slide, then rotate 90 degrees to land fakie facing down the hill.",,,
Rails / Boxes,Blunt,,,Black,3.0,Tail Press,Bluntslide,Rail / Box,"A slide performed where the rider's leading foot passes over the rail on approach, with their snowboard traveling perpendicular and trailing foot directly above the rail or other obstacle (like a tailslide).",,,
Rails / Boxes,Bluntslide,FS,,Black,3.0,Tailslide,Crooked,Rail / Box,Board slides with nose/tail elevated over the feature. Establish the feature position with a controlled entry; maintain pressure and balance through the feature and exit cleanly.,,,
Rails / Boxes,Bluntslide,BS,,Black,3.0,Tailslide,Crooked,Rail / Box,Opposite approach to a bluntslide. Establish the feature position with a controlled entry; maintain pressure and balance through the feature and exit cleanly.,,,
Rails / Boxes,Bluntslide,,,Black,3.0,Tailslide,Crooked,Rail / Box,"A slide where the rider's leading foot passes over the rail on approach, with the trailing foot directly above the rail.",,,
Rails / Boxes,Crooked,FS,,Black,3.0,Noseslide,Bluntslide,Rail / Box,Front end/edge leads the slide with the board offset. Establish the feature position with a controlled entry; maintain pressure and balance through the feature and exit cleanly.,,,
Rails / Boxes,Crooked,BS,,Black,3.0,Noseslide,Bluntslide,Rail / Box,Backside approach to crooked. Establish the feature position with a controlled entry; maintain pressure and balance through the feature and exit cleanly.,,,
Rails / Boxes,Crooked,,,Black,3.0,Noseslide,Bluntslide,Rail / Box,Front end/edge leads the slide with the board offset.,,,
Rails / Boxes,FS Boardslide Pull Back,,90,Black,3.0,FS Boardslide,FS Boardslide to Fakie,Rail / Box,"Enter in a frontside boardslide, maintain balance through the slide, then rotate 90 degrees back to regular stance facing down the hill.",,,
Rails / Boxes,FS Boardslide to Fakie,,90,Black,3.0,FS Boardslide Pull Back,FS Boardslide Sameway 270,Rail / Box,"Enter in a frontside boardslide, maintain balance through the slide, then rotate 90 degrees to land fakie facing down the hill.",,,
Rails / Boxes,FS Lipslide Pull Back,,90,Black,3.0,FS Lipslide,FS Lipslide to Fakie,Rail / Box,"Enter in a frontside lipslide, maintain balance through the slide, then rotate 90 degrees back to regular stance facing down the hill.",,,
Rails / Boxes,FS Lipslide to Fakie,,90,Black,3.0,FS Lipslide Pull Back,FS Lipslide Sameway 270,Rail / Box,"Enter in a frontside lipslide, maintain balance through the slide, then rotate 90 degrees to land fakie facing down the hill.",,,
Rails / Boxes,Front Blunt 270 Out,,,Black,3.0,Bluntslide,Nose Blunt,,"Backside nollie into a tail butter on the rail, chest tracking toward the hill as it slides, then a committed pop releases through 270 degrees back to regular — the mirror of a Tailslide 270 Out on the opposite edge.",,,
Rails / Boxes,Hardway,,,Black,3.0,BS 180,BS 360,Rail / Box,A backside rotation from the backside approach (take off from heel edge).,,,
Rails / Boxes,Nose Blunt,,,Black,3.0,Front Blunt 270 Out,Crooked,,"A Bluntslide performed on the nose rather than the tail: the front binding, not the back, sits over the rail as the board slides.",,,
Rails / Boxes,Pretzel,,,Black,3.0,Boardslide,BS Boardslide Pretzel 270,Rail / Box,Concluding a slide trick with a 270-degree spin opposite the direction in which you did a rotation during the trick's initiation.,,,
Rails / Boxes,Sameway,,,Black,3.0,50-50,—,,"Exiting a rail by continuing to rotate in the same direction the entry spin was already turning, rather than reversing it — the counterpart to the standalone Pretzel entry.",Bagel,,
Rails / Boxes,Switchup,,,Black,3.0,50-50,Boardslide,Rail / Box,A change in stance/orientation mid-trick on a feature.,,,
Rails / Boxes,Tailslide 270 Out,,,Black,3.0,Tailslide,Bluntslide,,"Nollie into a tail butter on the rail, body coiling as the board slides sideways, then one pop unwinds the coil into a 270-degree exit back to regular stance.",,,
Rails / Boxes,Transfer,Rail-to-rail,,Black,3.0,50-50,Boardslide to Boardslide,Rails,"Move from one feature to another. Use the feature as a platform for a controlled change in direction, balance, or airtime.",,,
Rails / Boxes,Transfer,,,Black,3.0,50-50,Boardslide to Boardslide,Rails,Move from one feature to another.,,,
Rails / Boxes,Wallie,,,Black,3.0,Ollie,Wallride,Wall / Feature,"Pop using a wall or feature. Use the feature as a platform for a controlled change in direction, balance, or airtime.",,,
Rails / Boxes,Wallride,,,Black,3.0,Wallie,—,Wall / Wallride,"Ride onto a wall or steep surface. Use the feature as a platform for a controlled change in direction, balance, or airtime.",,,
Carving,Carve Drag,Elbow,,Double Black,4.0,Carve Drag (hip),Carve Drag (chest),Groomed / Hardpack,Elbow contact with the snow during an extreme carve — effectively a partial laydown.,,,
Carving,Carve Drag,Chest,,Double Black,4.0,Carve Drag (elbow),Eurocarve,Groomed / Hardpack,Torso brought to the snow at full inclination; the edge alone is carrying the rider.,,,
Carving,Carve Drag,Two-hand,,Double Black,4.0,Carve Drag (hand),Eurocarve,Groomed / Hardpack,"Both hands on the snow through the turn, with the body fully committed inside the arc.",,,
Carving,Eurocarve,Toeside,,Double Black,4.0,Carve Drag (chest),Eurocarve (heelside),Groomed / Hardpack,"Fully laid-out toeside carve where the body is committed inside the arc and contacts the snow, with the edge carrying all of the load.","Laydown Carve, Extreme Carve",,
Carving,Eurocarve,Heelside,,Double Black,4.0,Eurocarve (toeside),Vitelli Turn,Groomed / Hardpack,Fully laid-out heelside carve — harder than the toeside version because the rider lays back with less range to adjust mid-turn.,"Laydown Carve, Extreme Carve",,
Carving,Vitelli Turn,,,Double Black,4.0,Eurocarve (heelside),—,Groomed / Hardpack,Named laid-out carving turn (after Serge Vitelli): an extremely inclined toeside arc carried so far round that the rider comes back up the hill.,,,
Flatground,Backside 540 Noseroll,,,Double Black,4.0,Frontside 180-In 360-Out,MFM Butter,,"A backside nose roll carried through a full one and a half rotations, entering and exiting on the same toeside edge — two edge changes instead of one, on top of the extra rotation.",,,
Flatground,Half-Cab Roll to FS Noseroll Nollie 360,,,Double Black,4.0,MFM Butter,—,,"A half-cab roll flowed directly into a frontside nose roll nollie — the heelside landing of the first trick becomes the launch for the second, so the two read as one continuous movement.",,,
Flatground,MFM Butter,,,Double Black,4.0,Backside 540 Noseroll,Half-Cab Roll to FS Noseroll Nollie 360,,"Named for pro Mark Frank Montoya: nollie into a tail butter, front roll to 90 degrees, snap back to the tail butter, then a counter-rotated frontside 180 out landing switch.",,,
